# Historical AIS Persistence & Authentic Vessel Forensics Engine

This plan implements a local historical AIS database, real-time telemetry persistence, CSV/GeoJSON dataset importer, and a "Strict Real AIS Only" attribution mode to ensure that the ML anomaly detection operates exclusively on real, authentic vessels present during the spill window.

---

## Proposed Architectural Flow

```mermaid
graph TD
    A["AISStream WebSocket Live Telemetry"] -->|Continuous Stream| B["LiveAISService"]
    B -->|Batch Insert| C[("SQLite: historical_ais_pings")]
    D["NOAA / GFW / DMA Historical CSV / GeoJSON"] -->|POST /api/v1/ais/import| E["AIS Import Parser"]
    E -->|Bulk Ingest| C
    
    F["Spill Attribution Query"] --> G["AIS Engine"]
    C -->|Query Box & Time Window| G
    
    G --> H{"Mode: Strict Real AIS Only?"}
    H -->|YES & Ships Found| I["Isolation Forest on Authentic Real Ships (MEASURED)"]
    H -->|YES & No Ships Found| J["Return Zero Suspects (MEASURED_HISTORICAL_ZERO)"]
    H -->|NO & Fallback Allowed| K["Augment / Fallback to Regional Corridor Dataset"]
```

