### Backend API & Schemas

#### [MODIFY] [vessel.py](file:///c:/Users/dhanu/SIH7926/backend/app/schemas/vessel.py)
- Add `strict_real_ais_only: bool = False` to `VesselCorrelationRequest`.
- Add `historical_source: Optional[str] = None` and `is_authentic_real: bool = True` to `CandidateVessel` and `VesselCorrelationResponse`.

#### [MODIFY] [ais_engine.py](file:///c:/Users/dhanu/SIH7926/backend/app/services/ais_engine.py)
- Update `query_vessels_in_corridor`:
  1. Query `db_service.query_historical_ais_tracks(search_bbox, t_start, t_end)`.
  2. If real vessels exist, convert directly into candidate profiles.
  3. If `strict_real_ais_only == True`:
     - If real vessels found: return authentic tracks with provenance `MEASURED_HISTORICAL_AIS`.
     - If no real vessels found: return empty array `[]` with provenance `MEASURED_HISTORICAL_ZERO` and an explicit note that zero AIS transponders were active in that corridor.
  4. If `strict_real_ais_only == False` and no vessels exist: fall back to regional corridor profiles.

#### [MODIFY] [anomaly_scorer.py](file:///c:/Users/dhanu/SIH7926/backend/app/services/anomaly_scorer.py)
- Support handling 0 or 1-2 authentic vessels gracefully without crashing Isolation Forest.

#### [MODIFY] [main.py](file:///c:/Users/dhanu/SIH7926/backend/app/main.py)
- Add endpoints:
  - `POST /api/v1/ais/import-csv`: Upload and ingest historical CSV.
  - `POST /api/v1/ais/import-geojson`: Upload and ingest GeoJSON.
  - `GET /api/v1/ais/stats`: Historical database statistics.

